# Backup Make App Files Before Editing

Make app files often have no git history (edited directly on the server via MCP, or
in a temp local clone). Before the FIRST modification of such a file in a session,
save a copy to the backup folder so changes are recoverable.

Backup root: `C:\Users\kacab\Documents\.cursor\backupFilesAI` (local-only, not synced).

## When this applies

Applies to Make app files: `*.iml.json`, `makecomapp.json`, component code
(connections, webhooks, modules, rpcs, functions), `*.imljson`, and any JSON/JS
code file belonging to a Make custom (SDK) app — whether local or fetched from the server.

## Never back up secrets

Do NOT copy `**/.secrets/**`, `*apikey*`, or any file referenced by `apikeyFile`.

## How to back up

1. **Local file edits:** before the first edit, copy the current on-disk file into the
   backup root, mirroring its path and adding a UTC timestamp before the extension:
   - Source: `<workspace>\connections\myConn\base.iml.json`
   - Backup: `C:\Users\kacab\Documents\.cursor\backupFilesAI\connections\myConn\base.20260625-193000.iml.json`

   ```powershell
   $ts = Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMdd-HHmmss'
   $dest = "C:\Users\kacab\Documents\.cursor\backupFilesAI\<relative\path>\<name>.$ts.<ext>"
   New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path (Split-Path $dest) | Out-Null
   Copy-Item "<sourceFile>" $dest
   ```

2. **Make SERVER edits (via MCP):** there is no local file yet. First FETCH the current
   server version of the component/code via the Make MCP server, write that content to the
   backup root (mirror app name + component + code type + timestamp), THEN apply the change.

## Rules

- Timestamp every backup so repeated edits never overwrite an earlier backup.
- Back up the ORIGINAL content (before your change), once per file per session.
- Preserve original formatting in the backup — never minify.
- Mention briefly that a backup was made and where.
